  <!-- STEPS -->
  <section class="reveal">
    <div class="sec-title">Methodology</div>
    <h2>Implementation Steps</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num">01</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Network Audit &amp; Traffic Baseline</h3>
          <p>Mapped existing flat topology using LLDP/CDP discovery. Captured broadcast domain size (single /16 subnet, 800+ hosts) and identified broadcast storm risk, bottlenecked uplinks and absence of traffic segmentation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num">02</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>3-Tier Architecture Design</h3>
          <p>Designed core-distribution-access hierarchy. Assigned dual Catalyst 9500s as core with VSS-like HSRP redundancy. Allocated distribution switches per building, access switches per floor with uplink port channels for redundancy.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num">03</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>VLAN &amp; Trunking Deployment</h3>
          <p>Created 12 VLANs with documented IP plans. Configured 802.1Q trunks between layers with explicit allowed-VLAN lists (no native VLAN leakage). Pruned unused VLANs from trunk ports to reduce broadcast scope.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num">04</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>OSPF Inter-VLAN Routing &amp; HSRP</h3>
          <p>Configured SVIs on distribution switches with OSPF Area 0 redistribution. HSRP deployed per VLAN on distribution pairs: primary active + standby with tracked interface priority preemption. Verified sub-second failover with continuous ping during switchover.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num">05</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>ACL Security Enforcement</h3>
          <p>Applied extended ACLs at distribution layer to enforce inter-VLAN policies: VLAN 30 (Guest) blocked from reaching corporate and server VLANs, IoT VLAN restricted to specific server IPs only, management VLAN accessible by network team hosts exclusively.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="step-num">06</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>SNMP Monitoring &amp; Validation</h3>
          <p>Enabled SNMPv3 on all switches. Integrated with PRTG for interface utilization, CPU/memory, and STP topology change alerts. Validated full topology via Wireshark captures, ping matrix across all VLANs and STP root verification.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

